{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvakPqJWyAVTzX7JQVea","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Recommendation: don't decide yet. Run a one- to two-week check on data you already hold, then commit or drop.**\n\n**Why not start now:** One lost deal and three requests is a signal, not proof. Without the CRM analysis, you can't tell whether SOC 2 is a recurring blocker or a one-off. Spending £60k and six months on a guess is the riskier option.\n\n**Why not drop it:** Mid-market HR tools hold sensitive employee data, and security reviews tend to get stricter as you move up-market. Dropping it may quietly cap your enterprise ceiling.\n\n**The check:**\n1. Tag the 140 lost deals, plus any currently stalled ones, for security or compliance as a stated reason. Read the notes, because the CRM's loss-reason field often hides this under \"other\" or \"went with competitor\".\n2. Add the three current prospects' deal values and stages, and ask sales how many deals stalled or were discounted over security questions.\n3. Compare the annual contract value (ACV) at risk with the £60k cost, plus the internal time it will take.\n\n**Suggested decision rule (adjust to your margins):**\n- **Go** if security-related losses and stalls would have paid back £60k within about 12–18 months of the report landing, or if the three live deals are large and winnable.\n- **Drop or defer** if it's rare and mostly small deals.\n- **Middle path:** if the evidence is mixed, consider a cheaper interim step. That could be a trust page, a pen test, a standard security questionnaire pack, or a SOC 2 Type 1 via a compliance platform. Ask the three prospects whether that would unblock them.\n\nI haven't seen your CRM, so I can't say which way the data will point."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3446,"cache_read_input_tokens":5036,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3446},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ad9cf477-b569-49cc-9509-2ac357aee6d5","uuid":"2ef19b71-7162-46d9-b6a4-f912cd56e9b6","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:09:37.023Z","request_id":"req_011CfvakPc9oNpw94V6wWjni"}
